.TH MDR 1 "2026-09-04" "mdr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdr \- lightweight Markdown viewer with live reload
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdr
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdr
renders a Markdown file with Mermaid diagram support and reloads it
automatically whenever the file changes on disk.
.PP
Three rendering backends are available: a native GUI window
.RB ( egui ),
a system webview
.RB ( webview ),
and a terminal UI with image support
.RB ( tui ).
When no backend is requested, the best available one is auto\-detected for the
current environment.
.PP
If
.I FILE
is omitted or is
.BR - ,
the document is read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend " " \fIBACKEND\fR
Rendering backend to use:
.BR auto ", " egui ", " webview " or " tui .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging (image resolution, mermaid rendering, etc.).
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Never access the network: remote images are not downloaded. Can also be set in
the config file with
.BR "offline #true" .
The flag only turns the mode on: it cannot re\-enable network access when the
config file already disables it.
.TP
.BR \-\-export\-pdf " " \fIPDF\fR
Export to a PDF file and exit without opening a viewer. Includes a linked
contents page, bookmarks, page numbers, images and rendered diagrams.
Contents entries include section page numbers with dotted leaders, verified
against the final PDF pagination.
Requires webview support and an installed Chrome or Chromium.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-toc
Omit the contents page when used with
.BR \-\-export\-pdf .
.TP
.B \-\-landscape
Use landscape A4 pages when used with
.BR \-\-export\-pdf .
.TP
.BR \-\-pdf\-browser " " \fIPATH\fR
Select a Chrome/Chromium executable for PDF export instead of auto-detection.
The MDR_PDF_BROWSER environment variable can also select the executable.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the config file. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/mdr/config.kdl .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-backends
List available backends and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Create a default config file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mdr/config.kdl
Default configuration file, in KDL format. Create it with
.BR "mdr \-\-init" ,
or point elsewhere with
.BR \-\-config .
.PP
Three keys are recognised, each mirroring the command line option of the same
name:
.TP
.B backend
Backend to start with:
.BR auto ", " egui ", " webview " or " tui .
.TP
.B verbose
Boolean, enables verbose logging by default.
.TP
.B offline
Boolean, never access the network.
.PP
Booleans use the KDL syntax
.RB ( "verbose #true" ", " "offline #false" );
a bare node such as
.B offline
on its own means true. Example:
.PP
.RS
.EX
backend webview
offline #true
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Render a file with the auto\-detected backend:
.B mdr README.md
.TP
Force the terminal backend:
.B mdr \-b tui README.md
.TP
Read from standard input:
.B cat README.md | mdr
.TP
Render without touching the network:
.B mdr \-\-offline README.md
.TP
Export a PDF with a contents page:
.B mdr README.md \-\-export\-pdf README.pdf
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B mdr
exits with status 0 on success and a non\-zero status if the file cannot be
read or no rendering backend is available.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage:
.I https://github.com/CleverCloud/mdr
.SH AUTHOR
Clever Cloud <opensource@clever\-cloud.com>
